1. split raw audio files into <=1s long segments per channel
    data/raw_sound_files => data/raw_audio_files_1s
2. split data into training, test and validation set (70:15:15, randomized selection)
    data/raw_sound_files_1s => data/test , data/training , data/validation
3. calculate reference values for psychoacoustic parameters
    data/raw_sound_files => data/reference_values/partial_df_1/XXX.csv (loudness, sharpness, roughness, TNR)
    data/raw_sound_files_1s => data/reference_values/partial_df_2/XXX.csv (SII)
4. merge them into a single references.csv
    # 1. append the partial_df2's on a per file basis together on a 2ms grid with the correct number of empty values and a correct time_index
    # 2. fix df1's time_index by adding empty values and moving them on the correct places on the 2ms grid indicated by the time_index (0 = 0ms, 1 = 2ms, 2 = 4ms, ...)
5. median 1s-chunk (with values moved direct one after another)
    data/reference_values/references.csv => data/reference_values/median_1s_chunk.csv

